t lines (since each line can have at most one point per column). We have 4 lines, so each line will get exactly one point from column 2. Let's see constraints.\n\nCurrent assignments:\n\n- L1: (5,1) (y=1,sum=6) and (3,2) (y=2,sum=5). So L1 currently has y's {1,2}, sums {6,5}.\n\n- L2: currently empty (no points assigned yet). It will get points from columns 4,3,2 maybe.\n\n- L3: empty.\n\n- L4: empty.\n\nNow column 4 points: (4,1) sum=5,y=1; (4,2) sum=6,y=2. They cannot go to L1 because of y or sum conflict. So assign them to L2 and L3 perhaps.\n\nLet's assign (4,1) to L2, (4,2) to L3.\n\nNow column 3 points: (3,1) sum=4,y=1; (3,2) already assigned to L1; (3,3) sum=6,y=3. So we need to assign (3,1) and (3,3) to L2 and L3 (or L4). L2 currently has (4,1) (y=1,sum=5). So L2 cannot take (3,1) because y=1 duplicate. L2 also cannot take (3,3) if sum=6 duplicate? L2 sum=5, (3,3) sum=6, distinct, y=3 distinct, so L2 could take (3,3). L3 currently has (4,2) (y=2,sum=6). So L3 cannot take (3,3) because sum=6 duplicate, nor (3,1) because y=1 distinct, sum=4 distinct, so L3 could take (3,1). So assign (3,3) to L2, (3,1) to L3.\n\nNow column 2 points: (2,1) sum=3,y=1; (2,2) sum=4,y=2; (2,3) sum=5,y=3; (2,4) sum=6,y=4. We need to assign each to a distinct line L1-L4.\n\nCurrent line states:\n\n- L1: points (5,1) (y=1,sum=6), (3,2) (y=2,sum=5). So L1 has y's {1,2}, sums {6,5}.\n\n- L2: points (4,1) (y=1,sum=5), (3,3) (y=3,sum=6). So L2 has y's {1,3}, sums {5,6}.\n\n- L3: points (4,2) (y=2,sum=6), (3,1) (y=1,sum=4). So L3 has y's {2,1}, sums {6,4}.\n\n- L4: empty.\n\nNow assign column 2 points:\n\nWe need to assign each of the four points to distinct lines. Let's consider each line's constraints:\n\n- L1 cannot take a point with y=1 (duplicate) or y=2 (duplicate) or sum=5 or sum=6 (duplicate). So L1 cannot take (2,1) (y=1), (2,2) (y=2), (2,3) (sum=5), (2,4) (sum=6). Actually (2,3) sum=5, duplicate sum, not allowed. (2,4) sum=6 duplicate sum. So L1 cannot take any of the four points